      "title": "Exact exhaustive verification of the fixed 536-integer coloring certificate",
      "summary": "The original deterministic checker exactly validates the fixed certificate and exhaustively tests all 71,824 relevant Schur triples through 536. The later verifier uses baseline data agreeing entry-for-entry with the certificate and independently repeats the baseline check. The method remains specialized to the fixed 536-integer, six-color format; missing LRAT payloads affect the separate local radius theorem, not this baseline verification.",
